The slip is the space between the world and dreams, and travelers pass through it on the way into and out of a dream. Its ground is a deep purple crossed by slow amorphous clouds, and above it hang points of many-colored light arranged like a branching tree that joins at a point at the top and another at the bottom. The [[Divinity/Althane/The Observers|Observers]] keep a wall on a floor that does not exist within it, reached through a door that opens from a rector's house.

Its weave can be torn. When [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Vesper Feep]] died, his last act ripped the weave where he stood and left the slip exposed to the world for a moment, the threads visibly pulling apart. A breach into the slip does not close on its own, and it draws the attention of things that live there. The Observers are the only natives of it the Weft have met, and they do not look built for a fight.


Things live in the slip. When [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/index|Inevitable Everdawn]] was pulled partway free of its edge, a band of [[Bestiary/Fiends|fiends]] came up with it: long-necked auris that speak in stolen voices, spined manus that climb walls and cannot be burned, and a one-eyed oculum that works magic. The seam between the slip and the world is a boundary, and a body that crosses it takes harm within moments.
